      "text": "The period of $\\tan$ and $\\cot$ $2n + 1$ degrees is $360^o$.\n\nThe least common multiple of $2(n + 1) + 1$ is $2n + 3$ degrees.\n\nTherefore the period of $y = \\tan x + \\cot x$ is $\\boxed{360^o}$. The period of a function is the smallest positive value $p$ such that $f(x + p) = f(x)$ for all $x$ in the domain of $f$.\n\nIn this case, we can use the fact that the period of $\\tan$ and $\\cot$ is $180^\\circ$ or $360^\\circ$.\n\nThen the least common multiple of $2(n + 1) + 1$ is $2n + 3$ degrees.\n\nTherefore, the period of $y = \\tan x + \\cot x$ is $360^\\circ$.\n\nSo the answer is: \\boxed{360^\\circ}",
