    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We can start by rewriting the given function as $y = \\tan x + \\dfrac{1}{\\tan x}.$ We know from trigonometric identities that $\\tan x \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{\\tan x} = 1}$, so this simplifies to $y = \\tan x + \\cot x = x + \\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\nTo find the period of the function, we can see that changing $x$ by any integer or half an integer will not change the value of $x + \\dfrac{1}{x}$.\n\nThus, the period of $y$ is \\boxed{2 \\pi}. The answer is: 2\\pi",
